														<r3d:remarks>Description:
&quot;The Database of Genomic Variants archive provides curated archiving and distribution of publicly available genomic structural variants. Direct submissions are accepted as well as published data. The DGVa is the primary supplier of data to the Database of Genomic Variants (DGV) (hosted by The Centre for Applied Genomics in Toronto, Canada).&quot;

The DGVa works closely with the Database of Genomic Variants (DGV), hosted by The Centre for Applied Genomics in Toronto, Canada and dbVar hosted by the National Center for Biotechnology Information in Washington DC, USA. These collaborations aim to improve community resources for the storage, distribution and analysis of genomic structural variation.</r3d:remarks>
